  "platform": "Sega Saturn",
  "summary": "Lundi and Lagi pursue an ancient airship through a rail shooter with branching routes and an evolving dragon.",
  "body": [
    "Panzer Dragoon II Zwei is Team Andromeda’s Saturn rail shooter, first released in Japan on 22 March 1996. Set before the original game, it follows Lundi and Lagi, an unusual creature he shelters against his village’s customs. When an ancient airship destroys the village, the two pursue it. Lagi begins the journey close to the ground before taking to the air. The player again aims the rider’s gun and the dragon’s lasers, while the flight passes through landscapes shaped by the machinery of a vanished civilisation.",
    "Some stages divide into alternative routes. Steering towards one branch changes the scenery and enemies encountered for the rest of that section, so a replay can follow a different journey through familiar territory. Threats still approach from several directions, with the radar helping the player decide when to turn the view. Shooting enemies also fills a Berserk meter. Activating it releases a sustained stream of homing lasers, providing a powerful answer when several attackers fill the screen and ordinary targeting leaves too much to handle at once.",
    "Performance affects the travelling companion itself. Stage results take account of shooting, damage and other measures, and Lagi evolves into stronger forms as the adventure progresses. The player can therefore see the results of earlier flights in the dragon carrying Lundi. Finishing the game also opens Pandora’s Box, an extras menu for revisiting stages and changing settings. Yayoi Wachi’s score accompanies a story told through animated scenes and the series’ invented language, giving the short shooting campaign another reason to be followed through to its conclusion."
  ],
  "story_headings": [
    "Lundi and Lagi",
    "Choosing a path in flight",
    "A stronger companion"
  ],
